    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "An appropriate form of **होगा** can be used as an auxiliary verb. It gives a future meaning or suggests a degree of uncertainty or probability. This is sometimes called the *presumptive* usage. Examples include:\n\n• वह सो रहा होगा — He will be sleeping (at this time tomorrow) or He is probably sleeping (but I'm not sure).\n• वहां रहती होंगी — She probably lives there.\n• वे जानते होंगे — He must know.\n• आपने देखा होगा — You must have seen it.\n\nMore complex examples show the same usage:\n\n• आपने देख लिया होगा — You must have seen (it) by now.\n• वे टाइप कर सकती होंगी — She can probably type.\n• वे आ चुके होंगे — He must have arrived.\n• इन्हें रहना होगा — They will have to stay.\n• हमें साड़ियां खरीदनी होंगी — We will have to buy saris.\n\nThe short form without **होगा** has a *contingent* meaning, often used in **if** clauses and with expressions of obligation:\n\n• अगर आपको ज़रूर जाना हो — If you really must go …\n• अगर आपका लड़का कल जा रहा हो — If your son is going tomorrow.\n• अगर वे खाना खाते हों — If they are eating.\n• यदि वह बाजार गये हों — If he has gone to the market.\n• शायद वे बाजार गये हों — Maybe he has already gone downtown.\n• शायद वे अभी तक आये न हों — Probably they haven’t come yet."
    }
